<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header"><h2>Understanding Massage Chair Features</h2><p>Premium massage chairs differ in the technology and engineering behind them.</p></div>
        <div class="edu-grid">
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>What Is 4D Massage?</h3><p>4D rollers move in four dimensions — up/down, left/right, in/out, and with variable speed. This creates a more human-like massage that adjusts pressure dynamically mid-stroke.</p></div>
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>What Is Zero Gravity?</h3><p>Inspired by NASA seating, zero gravity positions the legs above the heart. This reduces spinal pressure and allows the massage to penetrate more deeply.</p></div>
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>What Is Body Scanning?</h3><p>Advanced sensors map your spine's curvature and pressure points before each session. The chair adjusts roller position and intensity to match your body exactly.</p></div>
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>SL-Track vs. L-Track</h3><p>An SL-Track follows the natural S-curve of your spine from neck to lower back and continues under the glutes. Both provide more complete coverage than basic straight tracks.</p></div>
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>Heat Therapy</h3><p>Integrated heating elements warm muscles before and during massage. Heat improves circulation, loosens tension, and creates a deeper sense of relaxation.</p></div>
            <div class="edu-card"><h3>Air Compression Massage</h3><p>Strategically placed airbags inflate around arms, legs, shoulders, and feet. This rhythmic compression improves circulation and complements roller massage.</p></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

